  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ehancing Access To Essential WASH And Health Services For Conflict Affected Populations In Yemen</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Due to years of conflict in Yemen, millions of individuals are faced with increased challenges in accessing basic services. Internally displaced populations (IDPs) and migrants are often disproportionally affected by lack of water, sanitation, hygiene (WASH), and health services due to living in remote and often under-resourced settlements, and other barriers such as cost and availability. 
 
Under this project, the International Organization for Migration (IOM) is enhancing access to safe water through the rehabilitation and expansion of water supply systems that will cover the immediate water needs of an estimated 120,000 people, including IDPs and host communities in Yemen. Complementing this activity, IOM is hosting various hygiene promotion activities and providing community members with technical skills trainings to fill WASH-related labour gaps and strengthen community ownership and maintenance of the water systems.</narrative>
  </description>
